# Normalise line endings.
#
# This repository is written on Windows and built on Linux (Vercel, Render,
# Docker). Without this, CRLF leaks into files where it breaks things: a shell
# script with CRLF fails with `bad interpreter`, and a Dockerfile RUN line
# carries a stray \r into the command.
#
# `text=auto` stores everything as LF in the repository and checks out the
# platform's native ending for editing.
* text=auto

# Always LF, even on a Windows checkout — these are executed by Linux.
*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile*     text eol=lf
*.mjs           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf

# Never touched: a byte changed here is a corrupted file.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.woff2         binary
*.p12           binary
*.keystore      binary

# Generated. Collapsing these keeps a diff readable and keeps GitHub's language
# statistics pointed at the code rather than the lockfile.
pnpm-lock.yaml  linguist-generated=true -diff
